From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): let the host pause the clipboard both ways

A host that lets a session be watched without being controlled (a view
only mode) had no way to keep the clipboard out of it: while the
component had the focus, it went on reading the local clipboard and
sending it to the server, and on writing what the server copied to the
local clipboard.

`setClipboardPaused(paused)` pauses the clipboard both ways, or resumes
it. While paused, the local clipboard is neither read nor sent, and what
the server copies is dropped rather than kept for later, in every
clipboard mode; `sendClipboardData` is refused, and the initial
clipboard request is answered with an empty clipboard. Pausing withdraws
what this side offered (the server is sent an empty clipboard) only if
it is still the latest there, so that a paste there gets nothing from
here while a copy of the server's own is left alone. Resuming offers the
local clipboard again if pausing withdrew it, and otherwise only once it
changes, as usual; a copy the server made meanwhile isn't overwritten.

Which copy is the latest is known only from what the session hands the
component: a server copy in a format the session doesn't fetch (files
only, say) isn't seen, and pausing then withdraws anyway.
